# Pono @PACKAGE_VERSION@

A statically linked build of the [Pono](https://github.com/stanford-centaur/pono)
model checker for x86-64 Linux, with a script that runs a portfolio of its
configurations.

    $ ./pono --version
    @VERSION_LINE@

## Contents

- `pono`: a Python 3 script that runs a portfolio of configurations of
  `pono-bin` in parallel, each with limits on its CPU time and memory, until
  one of them answers. It needs PyYAML (`python3-yaml` on Debian and Ubuntu).
- `svcomp.yml`: the portfolio for SV-COMP, which lists the configurations to
  run for each logic.
- `pono-bin`: the model checker, which runs without any other files.
- `smoketest.sh`: prints the version and the usage of `pono`, then runs its
  portfolio for SV-COMP, and `pono-bin` with each SMT solver of the portfolio,
  on the tasks in `examples/`, and exits with status 0 if every run reports
  the verdict the task is named after.
- `examples/`: a MoXI task on bit-vectors with a satisfiable query,
  `sat.moxi`, and one with an unsatisfiable query, `unsat.moxi`.
- `LICENSE` and `LICENSES/`: the licenses of Pono and of the software linked
  into it.

## Usage

    ./pono --svcomp <file>

runs the portfolio for SV-COMP on `<file>`, a model in MoXI format: the
configurations that `svcomp.yml` lists for the logic of the model.
`./pono --help` describes the options of the script and the format of a
portfolio, which `--config` runs instead.

    ./pono-bin [<option> ...] <file>

runs a single configuration on `<file>`, a model in Btor2, SMV, VMT, or MoXI
format, and `./pono-bin --help` lists the options. Both print `sat` if they
find a trace that satisfies the query (violates the property), `unsat` if they
prove that none does, and `unknown` if they do neither.

